# Rejection-order review

Source: `src/contracts/reasons.ts` (REJECTION_REASONS, 17 codes) checked against `src/submission/submit.ts` (`submitResult` and `decide`).

## run_dir_invalid

Triggered when no run directory is given (src/submission/submit.ts:104), when the journal entry cannot be lstat-inspected (src/submission/submit.ts:113), when the run directory holds no `journal.jsonl` (src/submission/submit.ts:119), or, under the lock, when the journal has no `run.opened` record (src/submission/submit.ts:153).

## envelope_malformed

Triggered when the envelope file cannot be read, exceeds 64 KiB, or is not a JSON object. Parsed before the lock at src/submission/submit.ts:131, reported and journaled under the lock at src/submission/submit.ts:160.

## envelope_invalid

Triggered when the envelope parses as JSON but fails schema v1. Produced by `parseEnvelope` at src/submission/submit.ts:139 (reason passed through), reported under the lock at src/submission/submit.ts:160.

## journal_busy

Triggered when the journal lock cannot be acquired. Surfaces from `withJournalLock` at src/submission/submit.ts:181 (`locked.reason`), and from `readJournal` at src/submission/submit.ts:151.

## journal_corrupt

Triggered when the journal entry is a symlink or non-regular file (src/submission/submit.ts:121), when the journal does not replay cleanly (src/submission/submit.ts:151 via `readJournal`, src/submission/submit.ts:210 via `replay`), when a duplicate submission's accepted copy is missing or altered (src/submission/submit.ts:271), or when a journal write fails with `JournalFileError` (src/submission/submit.ts:397).

## run_mismatch

Triggered when the envelope's `runId` differs from the journal's run. Checked at src/submission/submit.ts:215.

## attempt_unknown

Triggered when no `attempt.opened` record exists for the envelope's stage, visit and attempt. Checked at src/submission/submit.ts:225.

## owner_mismatch

Triggered when the envelope's `agentId` differs from the attempt owner (src/submission/submit.ts:234) or, when both sides carry a pane id, the submitting pane differs from the bound pane (src/submission/submit.ts:240). Rejected at src/submission/submit.ts:250.

## attempt_closed_conflict

Triggered when the attempt is already accepted and the new envelope's digest differs from the accepted one. Checked at src/submission/submit.ts:262. (Same digest with an intact copy yields `duplicate` at src/submission/submit.ts:284; same digest with a broken copy yields `journal_corrupt` at src/submission/submit.ts:271.)

## attempt_stale

Triggered when the attempt's status is `superseded` by a newer opened attempt. Checked at src/submission/submit.ts:288.

## verdict_not_allowed

Triggered when the envelope verdict is not in the attempt's allowed verdicts (or is non-null when none are allowed). Checked at src/submission/submit.ts:294.

## artifact_out_of_scope

Triggered when the artifact path does not resolve inside the attempt's artifact directory. Delegated to `resolveArtifact` at src/submission/submit.ts:308, rejected with the returned reason at src/submission/submit.ts:310.

## artifact_missing

Triggered when the artifact does not exist or is not a regular file. Delegated to `resolveArtifact` at src/submission/submit.ts:308, rejected at src/submission/submit.ts:310.

## artifact_empty

Triggered when the artifact has no non-whitespace content. Delegated to `resolveArtifact` at src/submission/submit.ts:308, rejected at src/submission/submit.ts:310.

## artifact_too_large

Triggered when the artifact exceeds MAX_ARTIFACT_BYTES (32 MiB), decided from file size before the content read. Delegated to `resolveArtifact` at src/submission/submit.ts:308, rejected at src/submission/submit.ts:310.

## artifact_hash_mismatch

Triggered when the sha256 of the artifact bytes differs from `artifact.sha256` (src/submission/submit.ts:317), or when the published accepted copy hashes differently from the bytes read (src/submission/submit.ts:339).

## journal_write_failed

Triggered when the lock call itself throws (src/submission/submit.ts:176), when the duplicate record cannot be appended (src/submission/submit.ts:282), when the accepted copy cannot be published (src/submission/submit.ts:334), when the acceptance record cannot be appended (src/submission/submit.ts:367), or when a rejection record cannot be appended (src/submission/submit.ts:389). Mapped by `writeFailure` at src/submission/submit.ts:397.

## Verdict

pass

The implementation follows the doc-comment order of `submitResult` (steps 1–18): run directory and journal entry (1), lock (2), replay (3), opened run (4), envelope malformed/invalid reported under the lock (5–6), run (7), attempt (8), owner (9), closed attempt (10), stale (11), verdict (12), artifact checks (13–16), hash (17), publish and append (18). The envelope is parsed before the lock but its rejection is reported only after checks 2–4, exactly as the doc comment states. The internal order of checks 13–16 is delegated to `resolveArtifact` in `src/submission/artifact.ts` and is not visible from `submit.ts` alone; this review did not open that file.

